    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/provost-and-dean-of-the-college-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Provost and Dean of the College",
      "description": "Provost and Dean of the College - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Provost and Dean of the College Provost and Dean of College Full Time Permanent - Faculty Full Time Permanent - Staff Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites PROVOST AND DEAN OF THE COLLEGE The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, seeks an accomplished academic leader to serve as Provost and Dean of the College. Reporting to the President, the Provost serves as the College's Chief Academic Officer, directing the Deans of the College's Schools and collaborating with the Commandant's office to align the academic and military components of a Citadel education. The Provost will also collaborate with the college’s other Vice Presidents as part of the President’s senior leadership team. Founded in 1842, The Citadel is one of the nation's senior military colleges, located on a 300-acre campus in Charleston, South Carolina. The College is home to the South Carolina Corps of Cadets, numbering approximately 2,300 students, as well as The Citadel Graduate College, which serves close to 1,000 students through evening, online, and graduate programs. The Citadel has been named the No. 1 public regional university in the South by U.S. News & World Report for 15 consecutive years, and the No. 1 public college for veterans in the South for eight years. Gen. Frank McKenzie, a 1979 Citadel graduate, began his tenure as the College's 21st President in July of this year. Academic programs are organized across the Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business, the School of Engineering, the School of Humanities and Social Sciences, the Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics, the Zucker Family School of Education, and the Krause School for Leadership and Ethics, along with The Citadel Graduate College. The College maintains an 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio, and nearly all faculty hold a doctorate or the highest degree in their field. The successful candidate will bring a record of academic leadership, including experience with faculty affairs, curriculum, and accreditation, along with the ability to lead within a structured, values-driven military campus culture. Qualified candidates must hold an earned doctorate or terminal degree, possess scholarly credentials appropriate for a tenured appointment, and demonstrate a successful record of senior academic leadership at the dean level or higher. Experience with both a traditional undergraduate program and adult, graduate, or online education is preferred. Military experience is not necessary, but the Provost will wear a uniform and will hold the grade of Brigadier General in the South Carolina Militia (SCM). Applications, nominations, and inquiries should be directed to the search firm contact listed below. Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials to our consultant at the address below by November 1, 2026, for full consideration. Application materials must include a current CV and letter of interest. The Citadel Provost and Dean of the College Search Funk Associates 2911 Turtle Creek Boulevard, Suite 300 Dallas, Texas 75219 Email: Krisha.Creal@funkassociates.com Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
