    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/department-head-and-associate-professor-professor-of-accounting-or-finance-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance",
      "description": "Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance Accounting and Finance Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor, Department of Accounting & Finance Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business The Citadel – Charleston, South Carolina The Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business at The Citadel invites applications and nominations for the position of Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor in the Department of Accounting & Finance. This is an outstanding opportunity to lead a thriving undergraduate department of approximately 300 students and 10 full-time faculty members within an AACSB-accredited business school committed to academic excellence, principled leadership, and continuous improvement. The successful candidate will serve as Department Head while holding a faculty appointment in either Accounting or Finance at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor , commensurate with qualifications and experience. The Department Head reports directly to the Associate Dean of the Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business. The Opportunity The Department of Accounting & Finance seeks a collaborative, visionary, and student-centered academic leader who will build upon a strong foundation while helping shape the department's future. The successful candidate will join a collegial faculty dedicated to outstanding teaching, meaningful scholarship and professional engagement, and preparing graduates for successful careers in accounting, finance, and related professions. Working collaboratively with faculty, the Associate Dean, and other university leaders, the Department Head will strengthen academic programs, recruit and mentor outstanding faculty, enhance student engagement and career readiness, foster innovation in teaching and learning, and cultivate relationships with alumni, employers, and the regional business community. This position offers the opportunity to lead through collaboration, develop both people and programs, and advance a department that values excellence, integrity, continuous improvement, and shared governance. About the Department The Department of Accounting & Finance offers Bachelor of Science in Business Administration degree programs in Accounting and Finance and supports the Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business through teaching in the Master of Business Administration program. The department serves approximately 300 undergraduate students and consists of 10 full-time faculty members , supported by a talented group of adjunct faculty who contribute significant academic and professional expertise. As part of an AACSB-accredited business school, the department is committed to academic excellence, ethical leadership, continuous improvement, and student success. Faculty are recognized for their commitment to outstanding teaching, close faculty-student engagement, scholarly and professional achievement, and service to the institution and profession. Students benefit from experiential learning opportunities including the Student-Managed Investment Fund, the Bastin Financial Leadership Laboratory featuring Bloomberg technology, internships, undergraduate research, and meaningful interaction with faculty mentors and business professionals. Located in historic Charleston, South Carolina, The Citadel is one of the nation's most distinctive public institutions of higher education. The University's mission is to educate and develop principled leaders through a rigorous academic experience grounded in integrity, leadership, and service. Required Qualifications Applicants must possess: An earned doctorate in Accounting or Finance from an accredited institution. Qualifications for appointment as a tenured Associate Professor or Professor . A distinguished record of excellence in teaching, scholarly or professional engagement, and service appropriate to the applicant's academic rank. Demonstrated academic leadership with evidence of sound judgment, collaboration, consensus building, and successful faculty development. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, written, and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with: Successful experience as a department chair, department head, program director, associate dean, or in another significant academic leadership role. Experience with AACSB accreditation, faculty qualifications, assurance of learning, strategic planning, and continuous improvement. Experience with faculty recruitment, mentoring, evaluation, budgeting, and resource management. Demonstrated success in developing partnerships with alumni, employers, professional organizations, and community stakeholders. A leadership philosophy characterized by collaboration, transparency, integrity, accountability, innovation, and student success. Responsibilities The Department Head provides academic and administrative leadership for the Department of Accounting & Finance and works collaboratively with the Associate Dean, faculty, staff, students, alumni, and external stakeholders to advance the department's mission and strategic priorities. Responsibilities include: Providing strategic leadership and articulating a shared vision for the department's continued success. Recruiting, mentoring, developing, supporting, and evaluating faculty and staff. Promoting excellence in teaching, scholarly and professional engagement, and service. Leading curriculum development, academic assessment, program review, and continuous improvement initiatives. Providing departmental leadership for AACSB accreditation, including faculty qualifications, assurance of learning, and continuous improvement. Managing departmental budgets, faculty workload assignments, course scheduling, and departmental resources. Supporting innovation in curriculum, pedagogy, experiential learning, and student engagement. Promoting student recruitment, retention, mentoring, and career preparation. Building productive relationships with alumni, employers, advisory board members, and the business community. Representing the department within the School of Business, throughout the University, and with external constituents. Teaching courses appropriate to the successful candidate's discipline while maintaining faculty qualifications consistent with AACSB standards. The Department Head teaches a reduced load of two courses per semester , allowing continued engagement in teaching, scholarship or professional engagement, and service while providing effective academic and administrative leadership. Administrative support is provided through a shared administrative assistant serving the School's three academic departments. Application Process Applicants should submit all required application materials electronically through The Citadel's employment website at jobs.citadel.edu . Review of applications will begin at the start of the 2026–2027 academic year (approximately August 15, 2026) and will continue until the position is filled. Application materials should include: A letter of interest addressing the candidate's qualifications for the position and leadership philosophy. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of leadership philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references. Recruiting at Professional Meetings Representatives of the Department of Accounting & Finance will be available to meet with prospective applicants during the Financial Management Association (FMA) Annual Meeting and the American Accounting Association (AAA) Annual Meeting . Prospective candidates who plan to attend either conference and would like to discuss the Department Head opportunity or the accompanying Accounting and Finance faculty positions are encouraged to contact Wesley M. Jones, Jr., Department Head , at jonesw1@citadel.edu to arrange a convenient meeting. Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
