    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-physical-activity-courses-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Physical Activity Courses (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Physical Activity Courses (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Physical Activity Courses (pooled position) Health and Human Performance Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is currently accepting applications to establish a pool of qualified candidates for adjunct faculty assignments. These positions may be temporary, part-time, and/or on-call, with appointments made either immediately or as departmental needs arise. This posting is intended to create a pool of candidates for future part-time teaching opportunities and is not for a specific assignment or a full-time faculty position. Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate Required Physical Education (RPED) activity courses. Course offerings may include, but are not limited to, weight training, swimming, first aid/CPR, racquet sports, yoga, archery, golf, martial arts, and other physical activity and wellness courses. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must possess a bachelor's degree and relevant professional, coaching, military, or instructional experience in the subject area. Some courses may require applicants to hold appropriate professional certifications or licenses. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience. Relevant professional, coaching, or instructional experience. Current professional or nationally recognized certifications applicable to the course being taught. *Please provide your resume, cover letter, and names of three references with your application. Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
