      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Exercise Science (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Exercise Science (pooled position) Health and Human Performance Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is currently accepting applications to establish a pool of qualified candidates for adjunct faculty assignments. These positions may be temporary, part-time, and/or on-call, with appointments made either immediately or as departmental needs arise. This posting is intended to create a pool of candidates for future part-time teaching opportunities and is not for a specific assignment or a full-time faculty position. Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in Exercise Science, Strength and Conditioning, Health, and related disciplines. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must possess a master's or doctoral degree in Exercise Science or a closely related field and have a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Exercise Science, or closely related discipline. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Exercise Science or a closely related field. Previous college-level teaching experience. *Please provide your resume, cover letter, and names of three references with your application. Start Your Application First Name (required) 077e92b8 Last Name (required) c02d4dd0 Email (required) 0190ee28 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.