    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-psychology-pooled-positions-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Psychology (pooled positions) Psychology Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Psychology at The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is seeking applications for adjunct faculty positions. Courses taught will be at both the graduate and undergraduate level. Minimum Qualifications: Adjunct positions at the graduate level require a doctoral degree. A master's degree is required to teach at the undergraduate level. Courses taught will vary from semester to semester based on departmental needs. Preference will be given to applicants who have previous effective teaching experience. If you have specific questions please contract, Dr. Chip Taylor at 843-953-5320 or taylorc1@citadel.edu . *Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until positions are filled.* About The Citadel College: The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students attend the Graduate College, evening and online programs. Start Your Application First Name (required) 350b50c5 Last Name (required) 269f29b2 Email (required) defe89d8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the dec