      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Engineering Leadership and Program Management (pooled) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Department of Engineering Leadership and Program Management (pooled) Eng Leadership and Prog Mgt Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking applicants for an adjunct faculty position in The Department of Engineering Leadership and Program Management for the fall, spring, and summer semesters. Duties primarily include teaching college graduate courses in the Master of Science in Project Management curriculum. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a Doctorate degree in Business, Management, Engineering or a closely related field; with a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level project management related courses. Applicants must hold the PMP certification. Candidates must also have documented work experience serving as a project manager. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience. About The Citadel: The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio