    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-baker-school-of-business-management-and-entrepreneurship-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Baker School of Business - Management and Entrepreneurship - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Baker School of Business - Management and Entrepreneurship Mgmt and Entrepreneurship Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking applicants for adjunct faculty in Management and Entrepreneurship disciplines in the Baker School of Business. Our goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality adjunct part-time faculty members who share in The Citadel’s commitment to develop principled leaders in business. There are main programs where adjunct faculty may be employed to teach classes: Our traditional undergraduate program, which features face-to-face classes to the South Carolina Corps of Cadets Our part time undergraduate degree completion program, which are primarily working adults earning Bachelor’s degrees, mostly through online classes. Minimum Qualifications: To teach at the undergraduate level, applicants must have a minimum of a Master's degree from an AACSB-Accredited Institution in the appropriate business discipline or in a closely related field. Be able to teach in-person classes, on campus in Charleston, SC. Evidence of previous effective teaching experience is required. Complete Citadel instructor training and follow rules and regulations set by The Citadel Center for Excellence and Innovation in Teaching, Learning and Distance Education (CEITL&DE). Preference is given to applicants who meet AACSB Qualifications as a Scholarly Academic, Practice Academic, Scholarly Practitioner, or Instructional Practitioner. Official transcripts indicating education level and background check are required prior to employment. If you have questions, please contact Dr. James Bezjian at jbezjian@citadel.edu . This is a pooled position and roles are dependent on department need. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) 8f5a3b8b Last Name (required) d4b3daca Email (required) d68735bb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
