    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-modern-languages-french-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position) Modern Language Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel's French Program welcomes applications for adjunct faculty instructors in French. Course availability varies. Subject to experience, teaching assignments may include beginner through intermediate language instruction. Scheduling is typically flexible within the weekday hours of 8 a.m. and 3 p.m. The Citadel’s goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality part-time faculty members who are committed to developing principled, well-rounded leaders who appreciate the value of being culturally and linguistically proficient in world languages other than their own. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered. Minimum Qualifications: Native or near-native fluency in French Master's degree in French or a Master's degree in another subject with 18 hours of graduate-level study in French or an equivalent Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching at the undergraduate level Interested applicants should start by sending a brief letter of application and a CV to: Dr. Caroline Strobbe ( cstrobbe@citadel.edu ), Department of Modern Languages, Literatures, and Cultures, The Citadel. About The Citadel College The Citadel, also known as the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more.  Ranked #1 Public College in the South (U.S. News & World Report, 2022) for schools with up to a master’s degree, the opportunities are endless. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students attend the Graduate College, evening and online programs. Start Your Application First Name (required) 57ef0329 Last Name (required) 14bc1ac8 Email (required) 44b7c0e1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Gradu