      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position) English Fine Arts and Comm Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is currently accepting applications to establish a pool for adjunct faculty assignments. Adjunct assignments may be temporary, part-time and/or on-call and may be immediate or as needed. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered for part-time teaching or allied faculty assignments. The Citadel’s Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications is establishing a pool of applicants  in the Fine Arts.  Duties include teaching undergraduate course(s) in one or more of the following areas: Theatre, Cultural Preservation, 3-D Technologies, Photography, Photoshop, Forensic Photography, or other Fine Arts disciplines, based on departmental needs. Undergraduate courses are offered during the day in face-to-face or hyflex formats throughout the academic year (fall, spring, and summer). All adjunct positions are part-time, temporary, and per session appointments. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Abiding by and upholding the Citadel’s mission, policies, and core values.  Utilizing effective teaching and learning practices such as presentations, demonstrations, class discussion, and other appropriate modes of instructional delivery; preparing course outlines and syllabi in accordance with program standards and in collaboration with the program coordinator. Completing student assessments required for program completion; hosting weekly office hours; meeting all scheduled class periods. Being available to students for individual consultation; submitting midterm grades; recording class absences and submitting final grades by the specified due date. The Citadel requires faculty to submit midterm grades for undergraduate students. The Citadel requires faculty to use the Attendance and Class Absence System to document class attendance for most undergraduate students. Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s Degree in a related Fine Arts field (such as Theatre, Photography, Graphic Design, Studio Art, or Art History) is required to teach undergraduate courses. Previous effective teaching at the high school or college level is required. Exceptional interpersonal and collaboration skills. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in the field is preferred. Experience in designing courses and materials for face-to-face and online formats is preferred. Start Your Application First Name (required) a7c030c5 Last Name (required) e0e78727 Email (required) 28417088 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
