    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-marketing-baker-school-of-business-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty (Marketing)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty (Marketing) - Baker School of Business - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty (Marketing) - Baker School of Business Mktg Supl Chain and Econ Adjunct Faculty 2950 Add to favorites View favorites Adjunct Instructor Position in Marketing The Citadel’s Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business continues to grow!  The Citadel is ranked the #1 Public College in the South offering up to a master’s degree eleven consecutive years and one of the Ten Best Undergraduate Teaching Schools in the South by U.S. News and World Report . We have innovative new academic programs, and a new business building, Bastin Hall, that opened Spring 2021. The ideal candidate will contribute to in-person, face-to-face course offerings and asynchronous online course offerings in Marketing at the undergraduate level. The Baker School of Business is AACSB-accredited and offers a traditional residential undergraduate program to members of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets (SCCC) in a military-college setting an undergraduate degree completion program. Job Responsibilities: The Baker School of Business invites applications for an adjunct position in Marketing. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses using both traditional and online delivery methods. The teaching load for this position is one to two courses per semester. Opportunities for summer teaching and additional compensation may also arise. Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have an earned Master’s Degree in a business discipline from an AACSB-accredited university , have relevant industry experience in the discipline, and be qualified to teach courses in Marketing at the undergraduate level. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates holding a PhD or DBA from an AACSB-accredited university are highly encouraged to apply. Online teaching experience in Canvas LMS is preferred but not required.  Preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach one or more of the following courses: Principles of Marketing, Negotiations, Personal Branding and Networking, Professional Selling, Consumer Behavior, or International Marketing . Relevant experience in industry, the military, or other organizational contexts is preferred but not required. Next Steps Interested applicants should utilize the official online application website and please upload supporting documents to include: Letter of interest addressing the qualifications listed above A curriculum vita Evidence of teaching effectiveness Contact information for at least three professional references. Additional Comments: Initial screening of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This is a civilian, non-uniform, position. About the Institution The Citadel , also known as the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina . Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and a heritage of excellence in education, emphasizing leadership development. The Citadel provides a unique, residential undergraduate experience in a military-college setting. There are approximately 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Nearly one-third of our SCCC graduates earn a military commission in one of the five US Military Branches. Students can choose from 31 Majors and 57 Minors. The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students, including MBA students, attend programs in the nonresidential Citadel Graduate College. The Citadel is located on the banks of the Ashley River near downtown Charleston, and is close to great restaurants and shopping , and much more. Life on The Citadel’s campus is the best way to work in Charleston. Stop into the full-service Starbucks on campus before the day begins. Between the parade deck (Summerall Field) and Hampton Park, right next to campus, one has access to the largest amount of green space on the peninsula. Start Your Application First Name (required) 8a844a3c Last Name (required) 4f7b5b9c Email (required) 623c9fd5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 United States 843.225.3294 Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Student Types Corps of Cadets Graduate Students Degree Completion Students Veteran Students Online Students Schools Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business School of Engineering School of Humanities and Social Sciences Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics Zucker Family School of Education Department of Leadership Studies Next Steps Apply Now Application Status Request Info Schedule a Visit 360 Tour Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy C