      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry - Charleston, South Carolina, United States The Military College of South Carolina Search All Jobs Applicant Login Candidate Settings Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Home Benefits About The Citadel Discover Charleston New Employees Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry Chemistry Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolinas is establishing a pool of applicants to teach in the Chemistry Department. Our goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality part-time faculty members who share in The Citadel’s commitment to developing principled, well-rounded leaders. Duties may include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a MS or PhD in chemistry or similar field; must have a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level chemistry/biochemistry courses. College teaching experience is desirable. Necessary materials in addition to the online application (this can be attached to the online application) A curriculum vita Three letters of professional reference Start Your Application First Name (required) 22c02777 Last Name (required) 539c6d45 Email (required) ddbebf61 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs Grounds Maintenance Specialist Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking a Grounds Maintenance Specialist to work in the Grounds Division.  This role will report to the Grounds Division Chief and is responsible for the routine maintenance and enhancements of the landscape at the residence of the President of the college, to also include general maintenance. Dean - School of Engineering Charleston Provost and Dean of College The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, w